{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"squared error loss squared error loss","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md","fileName":"Squared Error Loss.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Squared Error Loss","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 00:13\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Optimization and Differentiation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Loss Function","Categorical Cross-Entropy","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"squared error loss squared error loss","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md","fileName":"Squared Error Loss.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Squared Error Loss","heading":"Squared Error Loss","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Squared error loss measures a prediction error by subtracting the desired output from the actual output and squaring the difference. Squaring removes the sign and penalizes larger differences more strongly.\n\nFor a predicted value of 0.2 and target of 1.0, the loss is $(0.2-1.0)^2=0.64$. It is a simple [[Loss Function]] for scalar outputs; classification across multiple probabilities may instead use [[Categorical Cross-Entropy]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Optimization and Differentiation","Loss Function","Categorical Cross-Entropy","algorithms.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Squared Error Loss.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"squared error loss squared error loss","